{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.StokesSymmetryConstantQZero","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.StokesSymmetryConstantQZero","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.StokesQZeroDTCount","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.StokesSymmetryConstant"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.StokesSymmetryConstantQZero.symmetry_reading_qzero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.StokesSymmetryConstantQZero.symmetry_reading_qzero","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/StokesSymmetryConstantQZero.lean#L73-L93","doc":"**The symmetry-constant reading of `S⁺(0)` is `3`.** Discharging the abstract\n`StokesSymmetryConstant.symmetryConstant_const` hypothesis at the base point with\nthe concrete (cast-to-ℚ) `Splus0` entries: the reading `(S⁺₁₂+S⁺₂₁)/S⁺₁₁` equals\n`3`. Because that reading is q-independent (the abstract lemma), this base value\nis its value at *every* q — the entire symmetry constant is carried by the\ndecidable q→0 matrix. Not an internal derivation of `3`; see the file scope. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.StokesSymmetryConstantQZero.det_qzero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.StokesSymmetryConstantQZero.det_qzero","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/StokesSymmetryConstantQZero.lean#L70-L71","doc":"**The second GGM identity (eq 65) at q→0.** `det S⁺(0) = 1`. Decidable. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.StokesSymmetryConstantQZero.eq65_holds_qzero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.StokesSymmetryConstantQZero.eq65_holds_qzero","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/StokesSymmetryConstantQZero.lean#L65-L68","doc":"**GGM symmetry (eq 65) at q→0.** For the certified `S⁺(0) = [[1,3],[0,1]]`,\n`S⁺₁₂ + S⁺₂₁ = 3·S⁺₁₁` holds with structure constant exactly `3` (`3 + 0 = 3·1`).\nDecidable integer arithmetic on `StokesQZeroDTCount.Splus0`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}